    "intro_html":  "Zanzibar built its whole economy on spices, and pilau is what that history tastes like at the dinner table. Red onions get cooked down dark, cumin and cinnamon and cloves go in whole-hearted, and the rice cooks in the same pot as the chicken so every grain ends up brown and perfumed instead of white and bored. One pot, one lid, and each bowl comes in at \u003cstrong\u003e{{cal}} calories and {{protein}} grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e${{cost_ps}}\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost).",
